Why this fork exists
====================

HomeLab: macOS VM 2000 (Sequoia 15.8) on pve needs IntelBluetoothFirmware
for its Intel AC 3168 Bluetooth (8087:0aa7).

The newest upstream RELEASE is v2.4.0 (Feb 2024). The Sequoia compatibility
fix landed 2024-06-24 ("IntelBTPatcher: compat for Sequoia ... the HCI
memory"), i.e. AFTER that release. Master is 2.5.0, upstream publishes no
nightly, and the only CI artifact expired 2026-04-15.

So the working kext must be built from master. This fork exists only to run
upstream's own CI workflow:

    gh workflow run CI --repo gresheff/IntelBluetoothFirmware --ref master
    gh run download <run-id> --repo gresheff/IntelBluetoothFirmware
    # take the Release zip

Pair it with BlueToolFixup 2.6.9 (NOT 2.7.x - acidanthera/bugtracker#2505)
and do NOT install IntelBTPatcher.

Built copies are archived on pve at /root/.
Full write-up: HomeLab repo, macos-vms.md.
